<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 14-AUG					     .</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 14-AUG					     .</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Winnie, with 125 mph winds, is centered 660 miles southeast of Okinawa, moving northwest at 10 mph. It is forecast to weaken but may still be a typhoon when it approaches Okinawa in the next few days. It will be watched closely.  </p>
<p>Cleanup from flash flooding continues near Hong Kong, China, in parts of northern India, and in Pakistan. China may see additional thunderstorms, but storms should be less heavy in India and Pakistan over the next few days.  </p>
<p>Nothing further at this time.</p>
</text>
